      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Colonel Edwin Drake drilled the first oil well in 1859, sparking the American oil boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://oilcitypa.net/oil-city/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town sits where Oil Creek meets the Allegheny River, a bend that gave the city its name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oil_City%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Derrick Publishing Company ran two newspapers, The Oil City Derrick and The News‑Herald, keeping locals informed during the boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
